    "created_at": "2015-07-14T00:43:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-07-14T00:43:16Z",
    "body": "> (However, I don't know of any use cases in web APIs for such big integers.) \n\nIIRC some web crypto APIs end up representing 64 bit ints as ArrayBuffers, and could have benefited from native 64 bit int support. But, then again, I remember being convinced that ArrayBuffers was a good idea. Maybe the API was more \"a sequence of bytes which could also in theory be interpreted as a 64 bit integer\" or something.\n",
